mantle rm481
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_berit_mudton
title the inn helper with the floating spoon
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor talk=quiet
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk balances_a_spoon_on_a_folded_napkin_like_a_boat_on_blocks
likes barley_soup singing old_maps misty_dawns
dislikes waiting night_noise
fears a_tune_beaten_flat_by_noise the_last_ladle_left_empty
hopes a_whole_quiet_verse_between_two_servings
topics food +0.6 home +0.4 lore +0.3 work +0.4
styles comfort=warm gossip=quiet refuse=dry tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# rests a spoon on a folded napkin as if putting a boat to bed, and hears a tune where the ladle strikes the rim.

words
oath! = Spoon overboard | A crumpled chart
saying! = Set the spoon where it can rest | Every tune deserves a landing
spoon = a long-handled spoon | my favourite spoon
fold = two ridges of folded cloth | a pair of napkin folds
rimnote = a low note from the rim | the ring round a pot
pencilshore = the pencilled outline of a bay | the wavery line of a shore
barley = a plump grain of barley | a little pearly barley
steambank = a low bank of steam | a curtain of kitchen steam
quietend = the end seat beyond the clatter | the seat beside the wall
restbar = a rest two beats long | a small silence in a tune
mistcap = a pale hood of mist | a band of low mist
dampcuff = a damp patch on my cuff | a half-wet sleeve
kindbeat = a steady walking beat | a gentle rhythm

any
opinion city for 1 : I'd miss the sound of spoons against a hundred breakfast bowls.
opinion merchants against 1 : Give me a measure that holds the same amount whichever side of the pot you're standing on.
opinion festivals against 1 : From an upstairs window the singing comes clear and the elbows don't.
opinion dole for 1 : A meal in a warm room can keep doing good quite late into the next day.
opinion drink mixed 0 : Cider goes down easily enough. Remember which tune you meant to sing before you order another.
opinion road mixed 0 : An old map makes fine company provided nobody makes the mistake of following it too closely.
opinion times mixed 0 : Look into the pot and judge what sort of week it's been.

grown
line greet : Welcome to the quiet end.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : There's space in today's chorus for an unfamiliar note.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. There's still silence between the first few bowls.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The longer tunes fit now.
line greet.return : I'm listening between the little clinks.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : There's the note this seat was short of.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Go on, the spoon can keep its own count.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Your voice travels very clearly at this hour.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come sit inside the curve, kin.
line again.open : A little rest and then the tune continues.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Friend, I've saved the wall side.
line farewell : Go easy past the stacked bowls.
line farewell.return : And save a second dry crease for my spoon.
line react.news : Tell it without the extra beat.
line react.news.new : First time I've heard that struck.
line react.news.known : Same words. A different rim, perhaps.
line react.news.doubt : I'd hear it in a quieter room before I trusted it.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : We've time for a silence after that.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That one deserves a chorus.
line ask.how : Any warmth left in your bowl?
line answer.how : It's been a day for small, well-spaced mouthfuls.
line thank : That made the load sit evenly. Thank you.
line deflect_thanks : The cloth needed folding anyway.
line sympathise : I've a seat that asks nothing of its occupant.
line reassure : Let the noise settle. You'll hear your own thought again.
line decline : I owe another turn at the cloth tonight.
line accept_decline : Fair enough. I'll put the ladle down.
line preclose : I'd like to finish before anything boils away.
line accept_preclose : We can set this conversation down quite gently.

scene spoon_boat
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I rest #spoon# across #fold#. | A spoon ought to go down as gently as it came up.
b : Why build it a dock? | Has it said so?
a : Keeps the wet end off my last clean stretch of board. | Often. Listen to one dropped in an empty pot.

scene quiet_beat
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give a tune #restbar#. | A pot singing on its own is generally asking for attention.
b : Why leave room in it? | You answer in tune?
a : So the next note has somewhere to arrive. | I fetch a cloth and lower the fire slightly.

scene help_at_inn
when topic=work self.workplace self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I like two clear steps between myself and the next laden helper. | The sweetest sound around #self.workplace# is the quiet just after everybody's served.
b : Even when there's a rush? | No thanks?
a : Especially when there's something hot between us. | A busy spoon is a perfectly civil acknowledgement.

scene work_water
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A sailor knows a tilted board. An inn helper knows where the broth went. | On the water I notice how a load inclines.
b : Which knows sooner? | And ashore?
a : Whoever's nearer the low edge. | Particularly if several loaded dishes are coming my way.

scene grain_soup
when topic=food self.likes=barley_soup
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #barley.capitalize# wants enough time to open without giving up. | I let the soup rest for as long as one short verse.
b : How can you tell? | What sort of verse?
a : It fits the bowl of a spoon without looking defeated. | One I can finish before somebody comes looking for supper.

scene map_soup
when topic=lore self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #pencilshore.capitalize# could just as easily be a ladle stain. | I'm fond of a chart showing a misguided island.
b : How do you tell? | Can an island get lost?
a : See if the ship has anchored beside a grain of barley. | On a page it can wander positively miles.

scene mist_open
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #mistcap.capitalize# lets a roof show before the room below it. | A misty morning gives the Works a gentler edge.
b : Why watch that? | Do you like it better then?
a : For a moment a whole roof goes sailing without its house. | I enjoy seeing an old neighbour's face change.

scene sing_under
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Set the first note low enough to reach without lifting a shoulder. | I can keep a serving tune almost under my breath.
b : Do you sing louder afterwards? | How would I hear it?
a : Once I've found somebody who wants the rest. | Watch the spoon move. That's half the song already.

scene noise_after
when topic=home self.dislikes=night_noise
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The night belongs to quieter instruments. | I begrudge any door that bangs after the last tune dies.
b : Name one. | Can a door spoil a good ending?
a : A spoon placed carefully beside a folded cloth. | Listen to how long people wait for it to bang again.

scene slow_queue
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The worst wait is standing there with a clean empty bowl. | Don't promise soup in two beats if the pot wants twenty.
b : What makes it worse than others? | Would you count?
a : Both hands are occupied and so is the imagination. | Up to nineteen, quite patiently.

scene works_song
when topic=home self.quarter=works
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the Works you can hear the great iron notes through the little kitchen ones. | I've found #quietend# even in a room near the Works.
b : Can you follow both? | Where would I look?
a : I pick whichever beat lets me eat in peace. | Behind something sound doesn't like going through.

scene debt_place
when topic=times self.owes=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A debt on a slip of paper sits surprisingly heavily in a pocket. | I count a payment on a dry board.
b : What's your way of carrying it? | Superstition?
a : Separate from my shopping list. Dinner ought to get a hearing too. | Practical. I'd rather a creditor couldn't contest a blurred figure.

scene mist_cough
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #dampcuff.capitalize# dries sooner than a catch in my throat. | I pause for breath when a musical phrase comes round to rest.
b : Does a warm bowl help? | Does it matter where?
a : Even supposing it didn't, I'd have ordered one. | To the music, yes. My lungs make their own arrangements.

scene brief_word
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : Heard it from #world.news_from#. #world.news#. | #world.news#. The telling came through #world.news_from#.
b : Is that how the tune went? | Would you add a chorus?
a : Yes. Leave the words in that order. | No. A single voice carried that much.

scene simmer
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : I've heard kitchen talk reduce till it's very strong indeed. | There's a bit of talk abroad and a good bit of steam in it.
b : Is it ready to serve? | How much will be left tomorrow?
a : I'd leave the lid on. | I can wait to find out quietly.

scene meal_stretch
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean weeks call for spoons that reach farther round a pot. | When food comes short I use the narrow bowls.
b : Is there more there? | Can they hold enough?
a : Sometimes the last good grain settles against the curve. | They hold the heat while somebody makes up a mind to begin.

scene new_wall
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd point out the seat where a newcomer can put a pack down safely. | Arrive at serving time and you find out how a room works.
b : Safe from whom? | By asking?
a : From somebody like me carrying hot soup backwards. | By seeing which few steps everybody keeps clear.

scene song_finish
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a whole verse to fit between two bowls some evening. | I'd like a good wide window over a very quiet breakfast.
b : Would a quiet kitchen do? | What would you see?
a : A kitchen with somebody listening would do better. | The mist parting in its own time. I'd take mine too.

story bowl_chart [topic=memories|food]
  : Once I followed a line across an old sea chart until it stopped at a perfect circle.
  : Thought I'd discovered a bay with an impossibly narrow mouth.
  b : Did the chart give its depth?
  : The circle fitted my saucer. The line was spiced gravy. Quite shallow as it turned out.

story spoon_hull [topic=memories|work]
  : I folded a cloth into a splendid little stand and balanced a spoon on top.
  : Then I loaded the spoon with broth to examine the trim.
  b : Were the folds high enough?
  : The spoon kept its position beautifully. The broth acquired a destination all over my apron.

story lost_verse [topic=memories|smalltalk]
  : I made a tune to remember the order of the bowls at supper.
  : Reaching the last seat, I found I'd composed a nice extra verse.
  b : Did you need another bowl?
  : I went back and ate the extra verse myself. Best arrangement for an enthusiastic composer.

rule @fold_clean
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Two folds and the bowl end's clear.

rule @set_soft
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Softly with that last dish.

rule @mist_top
when concept=bark here.weather=fog
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's a roof setting sail.

rule @tap_count
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Three clinks and a boot for the fourth.

dlg resident.hub : A quiet word will reach this side of the steam.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. You've come in exactly on the rest.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=dusk] : Come out of the bowl traffic and we'll have a word.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : You can speak from beyond that empty seat.
dlg resident.job [self.trade_words] : The post is #self.trade_words#. I get the warm things where they're wanted.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The report names #world.news_from#. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : That account's simmered quite long enough.
dlg resident.bye : Leave the spoon resting there. Happy journey.

graft resident.hub
choice Can a pot really keep a tune? -> low_note
node low_note
say Empty it and tap the handle gently. Fill it and hear the broth muffle the note. A wolf sings differently before and after supper too.
choice Which makes the better singer? -> well_fed
choice I'll listen for the handle. -> hub
node well_fed
say I'd pay the better singer in supper. That way both conditions can be tried and nobody goes hungry on account of the experiment.
choice A fair trial. -> hub
choice I'll leave the quiet seat free. -> bye
